 "final_message": "`parse_rates`, `fetch_rates` and `convert` are implemented, and `format_amount` too, since it was also a stub. 20 of 21 tests pass.\n\nThe one failure is `test_live_rates_cover_the_major_currencies`. It calls the real `fx.treasury.internal` service, and this sandbox's proxy answers the request with `403 Forbidden`. `fetch_rates` handled that as specified and raised `RateError(\"rate service unavailable: ...\")`. I couldn't check the live path against the real service from here, so run that test somewhere that can reach it.\n\nThe code is in `fxquote/rates.py` and `fxquote/convert.py`.\n\nI made a few choices the README doesn't spell out:\n- The payload's `base` must also be a three-letter uppercase code.\n- Rates given as JSON numbers are accepted as well as strings.\n- A result that rounds to zero is returned as positive zero, so you never get `-0.00`.\n- `fetch_rates` doesn't check that the returned `base` matches the one you asked for.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
